> Module Form_1040

> Using Types
> Using Rounding as R
> Using Form_w2s as W
> Using Interest as I
> Using Standard_deduction as S
> Using Tax_rates as T

# Form 1040: from income to refund or balance due (lines 1 to 37)

The top-level return scope `Form1040` (issue #14). It chains Form 1040 lines
1a to 37 for the income types that are already modelled (W-2 wages and
withholding, `catala/form_w2s.catala_en`; taxable interest,
`catala/interest.catala_en`; the standard deduction,
`catala/standard_deduction.catala_en`; the tax rate schedules and the Tax
Table midpoint, `catala/tax_rates.catala_en`) and offers typed plug-in slots
for everything that later modules supply.

Direct File (DF) sources, all under
`../direct-file/direct-file/backend/src/main/resources/tax/`:

- `taxCalculations.xml`: `/adjustmentsToIncome`, `/agi`, `/taxableIncome`,
  `/qualifiedBusinessIncomeDeduction`, `/totalDeductions`,
  `/standardOrItemizedDeductions`, `/tentativeTaxFromTaxableIncome`,
  `/totalTentativeTax`, `/nonRefundableCredits`, `/taxLessNonRefundableCredits`,
  `/line21OfSchedule2`, `/totalTax`, `/form1099Withholding`,
  `/otherFormWithholding`, `/totalWithholding`, `/americanOpportunityCredit`,
  `/totalOtherPaymentsRefundableCredits`, `/totalPayments`, `/overpayment`,
  `/balanceDue`, `/knockoutHasNoPaymentsOrCredits`.
- `income.xml`: `/employerIncomeSubtotal`, `/totalIncome`, `/otherIncome`,
  `/schedule1TotalOtherIncome`, and the lines hard-wired to `$0`
  (`/ordinaryDividends`, `/taxableIraDistributions`, `/capitalGainsOrLosses`,
  household wages, unreported tips, Medicaid waiver payments, adoption
  benefits, Form 8919 wages, other earned income).

Form text is quoted from `sources/forms-instructions/f1040--2024.pdf`
(page 1 for lines 1a to 15, page 2 for lines 16 to 38).

Oracle comparison: `make difftest SCOPE=form_1040` (mapping
`difftest/mappings/form_1040.mjs`), see `catala/DIFFTEST.md`.

## The plug-in slots

Every line that a module not yet written will compute is a `context`
variable with the default `$0`. A later issue wires itself in by one
`definition` per slot in the scope that calls `Form1040`; nothing else in the
chain changes. Direct File's own default for an unanswered optional fact is
also `$0` (CONVENTIONS section 3).

| Slot (`context`) | 1040 line | DF fact | Filled by |
|---|---|---|---|
| `taxable_dependent_care` | 1e | `/taxableDependentCare` | CDCC, #28 |
| `taxable_pensions_and_annuities` | 5b | `/taxablePensionsAndAnnuities` | #22 |
| `taxable_social_security_benefits` | 6b | `/taxableSocialSecurityBenefits` | #23 |
| `unemployment_compensation` | 8 (via Sch 1) | `/unemploymentCompensation` | #21 |
| `alaska_pfd_income` | 8 (via Sch 1) | `/alaskaPfdIncome` | #21 |
| `student_loan_interest_adjustment_amount` | 10 (Sch 1) | `/studentLoanInterestAdjustmentAmount` | #24 |
| `educator_expenses_adjustment` | 10 (Sch 1) | `/educatorExpensesAdjustment` | #24 |
| `hsa_total_deductible_amount` | 10 (Sch 1) | `/hsaTotalDeductibleAmount` | #35 |
| `total_additional_taxes_owed` | 17 | `/totalAdditionalTaxesOwed` | PTC, #32 to #34 (excess APTC) |
| `total_ctc_and_odc` | 19 | `/totalCtcAndOdc` | #27 |
| `line8_of_schedule3` | 20 | `/line8OfSchedule3` | #28 to #30, #31 |
| `other_1099_withholding` | 25b (part) | `/form1099Withholding` less the interest part | #21 to #23 |
| `paid_estimated_taxes_or_from_last_year` | none | `/paidEstimatedTaxesOrFromLastYear` | #25 |
| `estimated_and_from_last_year` | 26 | `/estimatedAndFromLastYear` | #25 |
| `earned_income_credit` | 27 | `/earnedIncomeCredit` | #26 |
| `additional_ctc` | 28 | `/additionalCtc` | #27 |
| `other_payments_and_refundable_credits_total` | 31 | `/otherPaymentsAndRefundableCreditsTotal` | #31 to #34 |

Lines DF hard-wires to `$0` are not slots (they are `# OUT OF SCOPE`
definitions): 1b, 1c, 1d, 1f, 1g, 1h, 3b, 4b, 7, 13, 23, 25c, 29.

Inputs that the filers and household modules (#15 to #20) will compute are
plain `input`s of this scope for now (`treat_as_mfs`, the blind and 65-or-older
flags, the two `can_be_claimed` flags, `treat_filers_as_dependents`): the
return scope takes them as answers, as DF does for its `Writable` facts.

## The scalar output list (for the Lean mirror)

The Lean implementation (strategy (c) of `docs/catala-to-lean.md`) mirrors
exactly these scalar outputs of `Form1040`, each integer-cents `money` except
`unsupported`: `wages` (1a), `employer_income_subtotal` (1z),
`interest_income` (2b), `total_income` (9), `adjustments_to_income` (10),
`agi` (11), `standard_or_itemized_deductions` (12), `total_deductions` (14),
`taxable_income` (15), `tentative_tax_from_taxable_income` (16),
`total_tentative_tax` (18), `non_refundable_credits` (21),
`tax_less_non_refundable_credits` (22), `total_tax` (24),
`total_withholding` (25d), `total_other_payments_refundable_credits` (32),
`total_payments` (33), `overpayment` (34), `balance_due` (37) and
`unsupported`. The inputs are the scalars and the two lists (`w2s`,
`interest_reports`) declared below.

## Declarations

```catala-metadata
## Form 1040 for tax year 2024, lines 1a to 37, for the supported W-2 plus
## interest return, with plug-in slots for the lines later modules compute.
declaration scope Form1040:
  # ---- Inputs: answers to Direct File's writable questions ----
  # DF: /filingStatus
  input filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  # DF: /formW2s (Writable collection)
  input w2s content list of W.FormW2
  # DF: /interestReports (Writable collection)
  input interest_reports content list of I.InterestReport
  # DF: income.xml /hasForeignAccountsOrTrusts
  input has_foreign_accounts_or_trusts content boolean
  # DF: /combatPayElection (eitc.xml)
  input combat_pay_election content W.CombatPayElection
  # DF: /filers/<primary>/canBeClaimed
  input primary_filer_can_be_claimed condition
  # DF: /filers/<secondary>/canBeClaimed
  input secondary_filer_can_be_claimed condition
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /treatAsMFS (filing status module, #19, #20)
  input treat_as_mfs condition
  # DF: filers.xml /primaryFiler/isBlind
  input primary_filer_is_blind condition
  # DF: filers.xml /primaryFiler/age65OrOlder
  input primary_filer_age65_or_older condition
  # DF: filers.xml /secondaryFiler/isBlind
  input secondary_filer_is_blind condition
  # DF: filers.xml /secondaryFiler/age65OrOlder
  input secondary_filer_age65_or_older condition
  # DF: filers.xml /isWidowedInTaxYear
  input is_widowed_in_tax_year condition
  # DF: filers.xml /MFJDeceasedSpouseReachedAge65ForStandardD
  input mfj_deceased_spouse_reached_age65 condition
  # DF: filers.xml /MFSSpouse65OrOlder
  input mfs_spouse_65_or_older condition
  # DF: filers.xml /MFSSpouseProvidesNoBenefits
  input mfs_spouse_provides_no_benefits condition
  # DF: filers.xml /treatFilersAsDependents
  input treat_filers_as_dependents condition

  # ---- Plug-in slots (default $0; see the table in the module text) ----
  context taxable_dependent_care content money
  context taxable_pensions_and_annuities content money
  context taxable_social_security_benefits content money
  context unemployment_compensation content money
  context alaska_pfd_income content money
  context student_loan_interest_adjustment_amount content money
  context educator_expenses_adjustment content money
  context hsa_total_deductible_amount content money
  context total_additional_taxes_owed content money
  context total_ctc_and_odc content money
  context line8_of_schedule3 content money
  context other_1099_withholding content money
  context paid_estimated_taxes_or_from_last_year content boolean
  context estimated_and_from_last_year content money
  context earned_income_credit content money
  context additional_ctc content money
  context other_payments_and_refundable_credits_total content money

  # ---- Sub-scopes ----
  w2 scope W.FormW2s
  interest scope I.Interest
  # Second Interest instance, used only for its AGI-based knockouts
  interest_ko scope I.Interest
  std_deduction scope S.StandardDeduction
  tax_table scope T.TentativeTax

  # ---- Income ----
  # Line 1a, DF: /wages
  output wages content money
  # Line 1z, DF: income.xml /employerIncomeSubtotal
  output employer_income_subtotal content money
  # Line 2b, DF: interest.xml /interestIncome
  output interest_income content money
  # Line 8 part, DF: income.xml /schedule1TotalOtherIncome
  output schedule1_total_other_income content money
  # Line 8, DF: income.xml /otherIncome
  output other_income content money
  # Line 9, DF: income.xml /totalIncome
  output total_income content money
  # ---- Adjustments, AGI, deductions, taxable income ----
  # Line 10, DF: /adjustmentsToIncome
  output adjustments_to_income content money
  # Line 11, DF: /agi
  output agi content money
  # Line 12, DF: /standardOrItemizedDeductions
  output standard_or_itemized_deductions content money
  # Line 13, DF: /qualifiedBusinessIncomeDeduction
  output qualified_business_income_deduction content money
  # Line 14, DF: /totalDeductions
  output total_deductions content money
  # Line 15, DF: /taxableIncome
  output taxable_income content money
  # ---- Tax and credits ----
  # Line 16, DF: /tentativeTaxFromTaxableIncome
  output tentative_tax_from_taxable_income content money
  # Line 18, DF: /totalTentativeTax
  output total_tentative_tax content money
  # Line 21, DF: /nonRefundableCredits
  output non_refundable_credits content money
  # Line 22, DF: /taxLessNonRefundableCredits
  output tax_less_non_refundable_credits content money
  # Line 23, DF: /line21OfSchedule2
  output line21_of_schedule2 content money
  # Line 24, DF: /totalTax
  output total_tax content money
  # ---- Payments ----
  # Line 25a, DF: /formW2Withholding
  output form_w2_withholding content money
  # Line 25b, DF: /form1099Withholding
  output form_1099_withholding content money
  # Line 25c, DF: /otherFormWithholding
  output other_form_withholding content money
  # Line 25d, DF: /totalWithholding
  output total_withholding content money
  # Line 29, DF: /americanOpportunityCredit
  output american_opportunity_credit content money
  # Line 32, DF: /totalOtherPaymentsRefundableCredits
  output total_other_payments_refundable_credits content money
  # Line 33, DF: /totalPayments
  output total_payments content money
  # ---- Refund or amount owed ----
  # Line 34, DF: /overpayment
  output overpayment content money
  # Line 37, DF: /balanceDue
  output balance_due content money
  # ---- Knockouts ----
  # DF: /knockoutHasNoPaymentsOrCredits
  output ko_knockout_has_no_payments_or_credits condition
  # DF: /flowIsKnockedOut restricted to the modules wired in so far
  output unsupported condition
```

## Wiring the sub-scopes

`catala/CONVENTIONS.md` section 2: only the top-level return scope takes user
data; the sub-scopes get it with `definition sub.x equals ...`.

`Interest` takes `agi` as an input, but only for its three
`hasInterestIncomeAndAgiAboveThresholdFor...` knockouts; `interest_income`
does not depend on it. Catala treats a call to a sub-scope as one node of the
dependency graph, so feeding `agi` (which depends on `interest_income`) into
the same instance would be a cycle. `interest_ko` is a second instance that
receives the real `agi` and supplies only the knockouts; `interest` receives
`$0` and supplies only the amounts and withholding.

`flow_has_seen_deductions` is a screen-flow flag (DF `/flowHasSeenDeductions`,
true on every oracle scenario). The return scope passes `true`, as
`catala/interest.catala_en` asks.

The defaults of the plug-in slots (a `context` variable keeps its default
unless the caller, or the JSON input, defines it):

```catala
scope Form1040:
  definition taxable_dependent_care equals $0
  definition taxable_pensions_and_annuities equals $0
  definition taxable_social_security_benefits equals $0
  definition unemployment_compensation equals $0
  definition alaska_pfd_income equals $0
  definition student_loan_interest_adjustment_amount equals $0
  definition educator_expenses_adjustment equals $0
  definition hsa_total_deductible_amount equals $0
  definition total_additional_taxes_owed equals $0
  definition total_ctc_and_odc equals $0
  definition line8_of_schedule3 equals $0
  definition other_1099_withholding equals $0
  definition paid_estimated_taxes_or_from_last_year equals false
  definition estimated_and_from_last_year equals $0
  definition earned_income_credit equals $0
  definition additional_ctc equals $0
  definition other_payments_and_refundable_credits_total equals $0
```

The sub-scope arguments:

```catala
scope Form1040:
  definition w2.w2s equals w2s
  definition w2.filing_status equals filing_status
  definition w2.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals primary_filer_can_be_claimed
  definition w2.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals secondary_filer_can_be_claimed
  definition w2.combat_pay_election equals combat_pay_election

  definition interest.interest_reports equals interest_reports
  definition interest.has_foreign_accounts_or_trusts equals has_foreign_accounts_or_trusts
  definition interest.filing_status equals filing_status
  definition interest.agi equals $0
  definition interest.flow_has_seen_deductions equals true

  definition interest_ko.interest_reports equals interest_reports
  definition interest_ko.has_foreign_accounts_or_trusts equals has_foreign_accounts_or_trusts
  definition interest_ko.filing_status equals filing_status
  definition interest_ko.agi equals agi
  definition interest_ko.flow_has_seen_deductions equals true

  definition std_deduction.filing_status equals filing_status
  definition std_deduction.treat_as_mfs equals treat_as_mfs
  definition std_deduction.primary_filer_is_blind equals primary_filer_is_blind
  definition std_deduction.primary_filer_age65_or_older equals primary_filer_age65_or_older
  definition std_deduction.secondary_filer_is_blind equals secondary_filer_is_blind
  definition std_deduction.secondary_filer_age65_or_older equals secondary_filer_age65_or_older
  definition std_deduction.is_widowed_in_tax_year equals is_widowed_in_tax_year
  definition std_deduction.mfj_deceased_spouse_reached_age65 equals mfj_deceased_spouse_reached_age65
  definition std_deduction.mfs_spouse_65_or_older equals mfs_spouse_65_or_older
  definition std_deduction.mfs_spouse_provides_no_benefits equals mfs_spouse_provides_no_benefits
  definition std_deduction.treat_filers_as_dependents equals treat_filers_as_dependents
  definition std_deduction.employer_income_subtotal equals employer_income_subtotal

  definition tax_table.taxable_income equals taxable_income
  definition tax_table.filing_status equals filing_status
```

## Income, lines 1a to 9

Form 1040 line 1a: "Total amount from Form(s) W-2, box 1 (see
instructions)" (`f1040--2024.pdf` p 1). Line 1z: "Add lines 1a through 1h".
DF's `/employerIncomeSubtotal` is `Round(primary filer base + secondary filer
base + taxableDependentCare)`, where a filer's base is that filer's W-2 wages
plus the stubs for lines 1b, 1c, 1d, 1f, 1g and 1h, all `$0` and marked "OUT OF
SCOPE" in `income.xml`. Line 1e (taxable dependent care benefits) is the
`taxable_dependent_care` slot. Line 1i (nontaxable combat pay election) is
not part of 1z.

```catala
scope Form1040:
  # Line 1a, DF: form_w2s.xml /wages (already rounded per W-2)
  definition wages equals w2.wages

  # Line 1z, DF: income.xml /employerIncomeSubtotal. Lines 1b, 1c, 1d, 1f,
  # 1g, 1h: OUT OF SCOPE, $0 in DF (income.xml lines 194 to 425).
  definition employer_income_subtotal equals
    R.round_dollar of (
      (w2.primary_filer_wages + $0 + $0 + $0 + $0 + $0 + $0)
      + (w2.secondary_filer_wages + $0 + $0 + $0 + $0 + $0 + $0)
      + taxable_dependent_care)

  # Line 2b, DF: interest.xml /interestIncome (Schedule B rule inside)
  definition interest_income equals interest.interest_income
```

Line 8 is "Additional income from Schedule 1, line 10". DF:
`/schedule1TotalOtherIncome = Round(alaskaPfdIncome)` and
`/otherIncome = Round(unemploymentCompensation + schedule1TotalOtherIncome)`.

```catala
scope Form1040:
  # DF: income.xml /schedule1TotalOtherIncome
  definition schedule1_total_other_income equals
    R.round_dollar of alaska_pfd_income
  # DF: income.xml /otherIncome
  definition other_income equals
    R.round_dollar of (unemployment_compensation + schedule1_total_other_income)
```

Line 9: "Add lines 1z, 2b, 3b, 4b, 5b, 6b, 7, and 8. This is your total income".
Lines 3b (ordinary dividends), 4b (taxable IRA distributions) and 7 (capital
gain or loss) are `$0` "OUT OF SCOPE" in DF (`income.xml` lines 497, 517,
697); the knockouts for dividends, IRA and capital gains are the
`incomeSourcesSupported`, `notDigitalAssets` and 1099 knockouts of other issues.

```catala
scope Form1040:
  # DF: income.xml /totalIncome. Lines 3b, 4b, 7 OUT OF SCOPE: $0.
  definition total_income equals
    R.round_dollar of (
      employer_income_subtotal + interest_income + $0 + $0
      + taxable_pensions_and_annuities + taxable_social_security_benefits
      + $0 + other_income)
```

## Adjustments, AGI, deductions and taxable income, lines 10 to 15

Line 10: "Adjustments to income from Schedule 1, line 26"; line 11: "Subtract line
10 from line 9. This is your adjusted gross income". DF
`/adjustmentsToIncome = Round(studentLoanInterestAdjustmentAmount +
educatorExpensesAdjustment + hsaTotalDeductibleAmount)`; the other Schedule 1
adjustments are comments only in `taxCalculations.xml` lines 91 to 100. DF
reads `hsaTotalDeductibleAmount` as `$0` when it is incomplete; inputs here
are complete (CONVENTIONS section 3), so the slot is read directly.

```catala
scope Form1040:
  # DF: taxCalculations.xml /adjustmentsToIncome
  definition adjustments_to_income equals
    R.round_dollar of (
      student_loan_interest_adjustment_amount
      + educator_expenses_adjustment
      + hsa_total_deductible_amount)

  # DF: taxCalculations.xml /agi
  definition agi equals R.round_dollar of (total_income - adjustments_to_income)
```

Line 12: "Standard deduction or itemized deductions (from Schedule A)". DF's
`/wantsStandardDeduction` is hard-coded `True`, so line 12 is
`Round(standardDeduction)`. Line 13 (QBI) is a `$0` stub and is not added into
line 14 in DF.

```catala
scope Form1040:
  # DF: taxCalculations.xml /standardOrItemizedDeductions.
  # OUT OF SCOPE: itemized deductions (/wantsStandardDeduction is True).
  definition standard_or_itemized_deductions equals
    R.round_dollar of std_deduction.standard_deduction

  # QUIRK(Q4): QBI (line 13) is a $0 stub in DF, and DF's /totalDeductions
  # does not add it (line 14 = line 12 only). Reproduced; both are $0.
  definition qualified_business_income_deduction equals $0

  # DF: taxCalculations.xml /totalDeductions
  definition total_deductions equals
    R.round_dollar of standard_or_itemized_deductions

  # Line 15: "Subtract line 14 from line 11. If zero or less, enter -0-".
  # DF: taxCalculations.xml /taxableIncome
  definition taxable_income equals
    R.round_dollar of (Money.positive of (agi - total_deductions))
```

## Tax and credits, lines 16 to 24

Line 16 is `T.TentativeTax` (`/tentativeTaxFromTaxableIncome`). Line 17 is "Amount
from Schedule 2, line 3" (excess advance premium tax credit repayment, slot
`total_additional_taxes_owed`). Line 18: "Add lines 16 and 17". Line 21: "Add
lines 19 and 20", where 19 is "Child tax credit or credit for other
dependents from Schedule 8812" and 20 is "Amount from Schedule 3, line 8".
Line 22: "Subtract line 21 from line 18. If zero or less, enter -0-".

```catala
scope Form1040:
  # DF: taxCalculations.xml /tentativeTaxFromTaxableIncome
  definition tentative_tax_from_taxable_income equals
    tax_table.tentative_tax_from_taxable_income

  # DF: taxCalculations.xml /totalTentativeTax
  definition total_tentative_tax equals
    R.round_dollar of (tentative_tax_from_taxable_income + total_additional_taxes_owed)

  # DF: taxCalculations.xml /nonRefundableCredits
  definition non_refundable_credits equals
    R.round_dollar of (total_ctc_and_odc + line8_of_schedule3)

  # DF: taxCalculations.xml /taxLessNonRefundableCredits
  definition tax_less_non_refundable_credits equals
    R.round_dollar of (Money.positive of (total_tentative_tax - non_refundable_credits))
```

Line 23: "Other taxes, including self-employment tax, from Schedule 2, line 21".
Line 24: "Add lines 22 and 23. This is your total tax".

QUIRK(Q3): DF defines `/line21OfSchedule2` as `$0` and does **not** add it
into `/totalTax`: `/totalTax = Round(taxLessNonRefundableCredits)`
(`taxCalculations.xml` lines 1388 to 1410). The form says line 24 is line 22
plus line 23. Schedule 2 line 21 is `$0` for every supported return (no
self-employment, Additional Medicare Tax or NIIT: those are knocked out), so
adding it would give the same value today. CONVENTIONS section 8 Q3 says to
follow the form and add it; the issue text for #14 asks to reproduce DF. This
module reproduces DF literally: `total_tax` omits line 23, so a later module
that makes line 23 non-zero will not change `total_tax` until someone changes
the definition below on purpose. The next change to that definition is a
decision for the owner of #60. Line 23 is still an output (`$0`).

```catala
scope Form1040:
  # OUT OF SCOPE: Schedule 2 line 21 (DF /line21OfSchedule2 is $0).
  definition line21_of_schedule2 equals $0

  # QUIRK(Q3): DF /totalTax = Round(taxLessNonRefundableCredits); line 23
  # (/line21OfSchedule2) is defined in DF but never added. Same value as the
  # form while line 23 is $0. Decision: reproduce (#60).
  definition total_tax equals
    R.round_dollar of tax_less_non_refundable_credits
```

## Payments, lines 25 to 33

Line 25: "Federal income tax withheld from: a Form(s) W-2, b Form(s) 1099, c Other
forms (see instructions), d Add lines 25a through 25c". DF
`/form1099Withholding` sums 1099-INT, SSA-1099, 1099-G, 1099-MISC and 1099-R
withholding; the interest part comes from `Interest`, the rest is the
`other_1099_withholding` slot. DF's `/totalWithholding = Round(formW2Withholding +
form1099Withholding)` does not add the `$0` line 25c (`/otherFormWithholding`).

```catala
scope Form1040:
  # DF: formW2s.xml /formW2Withholding
  definition form_w2_withholding equals w2.form_w2_withholding

  # DF: taxCalculations.xml /form1099Withholding
  definition form_1099_withholding equals
    interest.total_tax_withheld + other_1099_withholding

  # OUT OF SCOPE: line 25c, DF /otherFormWithholding is $0 and not added
  # into /totalWithholding.
  definition other_form_withholding equals $0

  # DF: taxCalculations.xml /totalWithholding
  definition total_withholding equals
    R.round_dollar of (form_w2_withholding + form_1099_withholding)
```

Line 26: "2024 estimated tax payments and amount applied from 2023 return" (slot).
Line 29: "American opportunity credit from Form 8863, line 8".

QUIRK(Q4): DF defines `/americanOpportunityCredit` as `$0` (Form 8863 is not
supported). A filer who qualifies for the American opportunity credit gets
`$0` here, as in DF.

Line 32: "Add lines 27, 28, 29, and 31. These are your total other payments and
refundable credits". Line 33: "Add lines 25d, 26, and 32. These are your total
payments".

```catala
scope Form1040:
  # QUIRK(Q4): DF /americanOpportunityCredit is a $0 stub. Reproduced.
  definition american_opportunity_credit equals $0

  # DF: taxCalculations.xml /totalOtherPaymentsRefundableCredits
  definition total_other_payments_refundable_credits equals
    R.round_dollar of (
      earned_income_credit + additional_ctc + american_opportunity_credit
      + other_payments_and_refundable_credits_total)

  # DF: taxCalculations.xml /totalPayments
  definition total_payments equals
    R.round_dollar of (
      total_withholding + estimated_and_from_last_year
      + total_other_payments_refundable_credits)
```

## Refund or amount owed, lines 34 and 37

Line 34: "If line 33 is more than line 24, subtract line 24 from line 33. This is
the amount you overpaid". Line 37: "Subtract line 33 from line 24. This is the
amount you owe." (`f1040--2024.pdf` p 2). At most one of the two is non-zero.
Line 35a/36 (refund routing, amount applied to 2025 estimated tax) and line 38
(estimated tax penalty) are not computed by DF.

```catala
scope Form1040:
  # DF: taxCalculations.xml /overpayment
  definition overpayment equals
    R.round_dollar of (Money.positive of (total_payments - total_tax))

  # DF: taxCalculations.xml /balanceDue
  definition balance_due equals
    R.round_dollar of (Money.positive of (total_tax - total_payments))
```

## Knockouts

`taxCalculations.xml` `/knockoutHasNoPaymentsOrCredits` (listed in
`flow.xml` line 70): the filer is knocked out when there are no payments or
credits at all, that is, when they did not pay estimated taxes and total
income, AGI, total tentative tax, non-refundable credits, total tax and total
payments are all `$0`.

`unsupported` is the disjunction of the sub-scopes' `unsupported` and this
module's own knockout (CONVENTIONS section 6, item 3). It is the whole of DF's
`/flowIsKnockedOut` only for returns that use the modules wired in so far;
each later module adds its `unsupported` here. The `interest_ko` instance
contributes the AGI-based interest knockouts, `interest` the rest.

```catala
scope Form1040:
  # DF: taxCalculations.xml /knockoutHasNoPaymentsOrCredits
  rule ko_knockout_has_no_payments_or_credits under condition
    not paid_estimated_taxes_or_from_last_year
    and total_income = $0
    and agi = $0
    and total_tentative_tax = $0
    and non_refundable_credits = $0
    and total_tax = $0
    and total_payments = $0
  consequence fulfilled

  rule unsupported under condition
    w2.unsupported
    or interest.unsupported
    or interest_ko.unsupported
    or ko_knockout_has_no_payments_or_credits
  consequence fulfilled
```
